    id 79
    label "zu499ocrEHo"
    step 0
    date "2017-10-07T03:05:08Z"
    title "Nanotechnology: Where Dermatology Meets Science Fiction"
    description "Nanotechnology is used to develop cosmetics and skin care products which contain super small particles designed to do a certain job in the skin. For example, sunscreens can contain zinc oxide and/or titanium dioxide nanoparticles to block ultraviolet rays while minimizing the white coating on the skin. When you see the words &#8220;invisible&#8221; or &#8220;sheer&#8221; on sunscreen labels, it is likely based on nanotechnology. I bet many of the products you use incorporate nanotechnology. While it's certainly cool and has a sci fi feel, is nanotechnology safe? Find out all about this trending topic right here!"
    channeltitle "Dr. Whitney Bowe"
    channelid "UCyIUAG-jiOxs2IGMvGyBnHw"
