    step 0
    date "2021-04-28T13:30:05Z"
    title "Nanotechnology - The Future Technology | Nanochemistry | Nanoscience"
    description "This video gives you an introduction to Nanochemistry, a combination of Nanoscience and Nanotechnology.&#10;&#10;00:00 Introduction to Nanochemistry&#10;00:35 Invention of Nanotechnology&#10;01:00 Molecular Nanotechnology&#10;01:22 Machines can be manufactured at Nanoscale&#10;01:45 Scanning Tunnel Microscope&#10;02:25 Quantum Tunneling&#10;02:50 Conclusion&#10;&#10;In 1959, an American physicist, Richard Feynman came up with the concept &#34;There is plenty of space at the bottom&#8221;, in which, he believed that technology and machines can be manufactured at nanoscale.&#10;&#10;In 2017 can you imagine that we are able to manufacture transistors at the size of 7 nanometers? Which is 200 times smaller than the HIV virus and 500 times smaller than your red blood cell.&#10;&#10;Scientists believe, when a transistor is smaller than 7nm, it exhibits a property called Quantum Tunneling.&#10;&#10;Now we will dive into Nanochemistry.&#10;&#10;Subscribe to our channel for more videos. Press the bell icon for personalized notifications to our videos.&#10;&#10;The Voice of Aftertutor:&#10;NaturalReaders: https://www.naturalreaders.com/&#10;&#10;The music of the video here: &#10;Audioblocks: https://www.audioblocks.com/"
