    step 0
    date "2020-07-22T13:27:26Z"
    title "Nanotechnology/Best courses after Plus two/12th/Malayalam/Nanotechnology/India/UK/USA/Canada/Abroad"
    description "Nanotechnology after Plus two.  Which is the best university for Nanotechnology in India and abroad.  What are the admission requirements for Nanotechnology...&#10;Nanotechnology is the branch of Technology. It deals with the study of extremely small things and can be used across all the other science fields, such as chemistry, biology, physics, materials science, and engineering.&#10;Nanotechnology is the branch of Technology. It deals with the study of extremely small things and can be used across all the other science fields, such as chemistry, biology, physics, materials science, and engineering.&#10;It has a huge scope in the upcoming generations. It is the third highest booming field when compared with IT and Internet. In India, Bangalore and Chennai are the manufacturing hub for IT and Medicine. The Indian government has already started Nanoscience and Nanotechnology initiatives and various funding agencies like the Department of Science and Technology.&#10;One can find job as nanotechnologists; specialists or scientists. The areas where a nanotechnologist can seek employment include biotechnology, agriculture, food, genetics, space research, medicine and so on. Job opportunities are also available in National Physical Laboratory, Indian Institute of Astrophysics etc. Candidates with Ph.D can also join as faculty members in Universities and colleges or research fields.&#10;What are the job roles for Nanotechnology?&#10;Nanotechnologist &#10;Scientist &#10;Researcher&#10; Professor &#10;Engineer &#10;Medical Scientist &#10;Food Scientist&#10;Who can study this course?&#10;Candidates with excellent marks in 10+2 examination in science discipline. &#10;Candidates with Bachelor's degree in science / biotechnology / nanotechnology.&#10;Industries / Companies / who hire these professionals:&#10;Electronics / Semiconductor Industry&#10; Manufacturing Industries &#10;Biotechnology &#10;Medical Fields &#10;Pharmaceuticals &#10;Environmental &#10;Universities &#10;Product based companies (food) &#10;Research Laboratory&#10;Top Colleges in India offering Nanotechnology:&#10;Department of Physics, IISc, Bangalore&#10;Indian Institute of Technology, Delhi &#10;Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur&#10;School of Nano Science and Technology, NIT, Calicut &#10;Amity Institute of Nano-Technology, Amity University, Noida&#10;Top Colleges in abroad offering Nanotechnology:&#10;University of California, Berkeley &#10;Arizona State University,  &#10;Harvard University, &#10;Columbia University &#10;Northwestern University&#10;Colleges in Kerala offering Nanotechnology&#10;NIT Calicut &#10;College of Engineering&#160;, Thiruvananthapuram&#10;3  Amal Jyothi College of Engineering - AJCE&#10;     Kottayam&#10;For more videos please watch:&#10;https://youtu.be/OJgzu-QBffU&#10;https://youtu.be/ZMguSJoESMc&#10;https://youtu.be/obl7gYoMHFM&#10;https://youtu.be/29JBL-m87eY&#10;https://youtu.be/YFS55MGA76c&#10;https://youtu.be/LNdfKcySL8U&#10;https://youtu.be/wu18gj7Ic1I&#10;https://youtu.be/Lc_ox5SQFkw&#10;https://youtu.be/QEdpTfXkXrU&#10;https://youtu.be/hnB85Y5-F3Y&#10;https://youtu.be/4DrS3TxpabY&#10;https://youtu.be/iNkUjDzlf9I&#10;https://youtu.be/DBRaSevK9Z8&#10;https://youtu.be/fQacgbEqEvc&#10;https://youtu.be/DeFQSxMZNT4&#10;https://youtu.be/_ZbylG6io3w"
