    id 202
    label "OhalFgj6LJY"
    step 0
    date "2020-07-27T18:15:12Z"
    title "MCQ on Nanomaterials and Nanotechnology"
    description "This video lecture is an #online #quiz based on #Multiple_Choice_Questions (#MCQs) on #Nanoscience  #Nanomaterials and #Nanotechnology. &#10;#Nanomaterials are materials which are made particles having at least one dimension in between 1 to 100 nm.&#10;A #nanometer (nm) is #one-billionth of a meter, smaller than the wavelength of visible light and a #hundred-thousandth the width of a #human hair. &#10;Nanotechnology is the manipulation of matter on a near-atomic scale to produce new structures, materials and devices. The technology promises scientific advancement in many sectors such as medicine, consumer products, energy, materials and manufacturing. Nanotechnology is generally defined as engineered structures, devices, and systems. &#10;#Nanomaterials are defined as those things that have a length scale between 1 and 100 nanometers. &#10;At this size, materials begin to exhibit unique properties that affect physical, chemical, and biological behavior. Researching, developing, and utilizing these properties is at the heart of new technology. As small as a nanometer is, it's still large compared to the atomic scale. An atom has a diameter of about 0.1 nm. An atom's nucleus is much smaller -- about 0.00001 nm. &#10;In 1959, physicist and future #Nobel_prize winner #Richard_Feynman gave a lecture to the #American #Physical #Society called &#34;#There's_Plenty_of_Room_at_the_Bottom.&#34; The focus of his speech was about the field of #miniaturization and how he believed man would create increasingly smaller, powerful devices.&#10;As the #surface_area_to_volume_ratio of the nanomaterials increases, their surface becomes more reactive on itself and other systems. The size of the nanomaterials plays a significant role in their pharmacological behavior.&#10;&#10;In 1986, #K._Eric_Drexler wrote &#34;Engines of Creation&#34; and introduced the term nanotechnology. &#10;Scientific research really expanded over the last decade. According to https://economictimes.indiatimes.com, More than 10,000 patents on nanotechnology have been filed with the US patent office. &#10;Global nanotechnology business is expected to be around $125 billion by 2024, with startups to large companies, including GE, Intel, Samsung, BASF and AkzoNobel, developing products and solutions around nanotechnology.&#10;&#10;   #Electric_Dipole_and_Electric_Potential due_to_short_Dipole_ at_some_general_point&#10;https://youtu.be/bYev_o_44IM&#10;&#10;Full Wave Rectifier&#10;    https://youtu.be/rs1mmPNuJoY&#10;&#10;MCQs on Nanomaterials and Nanotechnology&#10;https://youtu.be/OhalFgj6LJY&#10;&#10;Feedback in Amplifier &#10;https://youtu.be/bA9GKaWswto&#10;&#10;Difference  between an  Amplifier and an Oscillator&#10;https://youtu.be/R7vTHxO95-I&#10;&#10;Hartley  Oscillator&#10;https://youtu.be/iw4diKqtASM&#10;&#10;Oscillators Fundamentals and Hartley Oscillator&#10;https://youtu.be/2unh9OiiKNg&#10;&#10;Feedback in Amplifiers&#10;https://youtu.be/Y1MY_ymzBc0"
    channeltitle "Physics-DyanMantra"
