    step 0
    date "2022-04-15T17:49:19Z"
    title "HDIAC Webinar: Nanotechnology in Combat Casualty Care: State of the Art and Emerging Trends"
    description "For over two decades, the government has invested heavily in nanotechnology research, and the broad applicability of advances in the field holds great promise to improve combat casualty care (CCC). Because of this broad scope, however, no single source exists that comprehensively assesses the current and potential applications of nanotechnology to military health service support, especially CCC.  This webinar will present preliminary findings of an ongoing state-of-the-art report being conducted by HDIAC to evaluate the current and potential uses of nanotechnology to improve CCC. Primarily, the session will review current trends in relevant applied and translational research, commercially available products, existing research gaps, and technical and policy-related challenges of implementation.&#10;&#10;https://hdiac.org/webinars/nanotechnology-in-combat-casualty-care-state-of-the-art-and-emerging-trends/&#10;&#10;Connect with HDIAC online: &#10;&#10;Web | www.hdiac.org/ &#10;Facebook | www.facebook.com/DoDHDIAC/ &#10;Twitter | www.twitter.com/DoD_HDIAC &#10;Instagram www.instagram.com/dod_hdiac/ &#10;LinkedIn | https://www.linkedin.com/company/dodhdiac"
