    date "2022-04-17T00:44:03Z"
    title "Hepatic Tissue Engineering and Cancer Nanotechnology"
    description "This video explores the use of hepatic tissue engineering and cancer nanotechnology within different species through experiments done by Dr. Bhatia and her team in vivo and in vitro.&#10;&#10;This video was made by McMaster University students Marwo Suleiman, Abigail Jacob, Jaanuni Shanjith, and Harrisan Sivendran in collaboration with the McMaster Demystifying Medicine Program. &#10;&#10;Subscribe to the McMaster Demystifying Medicine Youtube channel: https://www.youtube.com/DemystifyingMedicine&#10;&#10;This video is provided for general and educational information only. Please consult your health care provider for information about your health.&#10;&#10;Copyright McMaster University 2022&#10;&#10;#DemystifyingMedicine &#10;&#10;References:&#10;Silva, M. I. D., Sallinen, V., Lemstr&#246;m, K., Midtvedt, K., Ulloa, C., Immer, F., Weissenbacher, A., Vallant, N., Basic-Jukic, N., Tanabe, K., Papatheodoridis, G., &#8230; Loupy, A. (2021). COVID-19 pandemic and worldwide organ transplantation: A population-based study. The Lancet Public Health, 6(10), e709&#8211;e719. https://doi.org/10.1016/S2468-2667(21)00200-0&#10;&#10;Benefits of Nanotechnology for Cancer&#8212;National Cancer Institute (nciglobal,ncienterprise). (2017, August 8). [CgvArticle]. https://www.cancer.gov/nano/cancer-nanotechnology/benefits&#10;&#10;Bhatia, S. (2022, March 22). Tiny Technologies and Medicine: From Hepatic Tissue Engineering to Cancer Nanotechnology [video file] Retrieved from https://videocast.nih.gov/watch=44231&#10;&#10;Kulig, K. M., &#38; Vacanti, J. P. (2004). Hepatic tissue engineering. Transplant Immunology, 12(3&#8211;4), 303&#8211;310. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trim.2003.12.005&#10;&#10;Organ Donation Statistics | organdonor.gov. (n.d.). Retrieved April 4, 2022, from https://www.organdonor.gov/learn/organ-donation-statistics&#10;&#10;Moon, A. M., Singal, A. G., &#38; Tapper, E. B. (2020). Contemporary Epidemiology of Chronic Liver Disease and Cirrhosis. Clinical Gastroenterology and Hepatology, 18(12), 2650&#8211;2666. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cgh.2019.07.060&#10;&#10;New data show organ transplants fell by 31% worldwide during COVID-19 pandemic. (n.d.). Retrieved April 4, 2022, from https://www.healio.com/news/nephrology/20210908/new-data-show-organ-transplants-fell-by-31-worldwide-during-covid19-pandemic&#10;&#10;Simmerling, M. (2007). Beyond Scarcity: Poverty as a Contraindication for Organ Transplantation. AMA Journal of Ethics, 9(6), 441&#8211;445. https://doi.org/10.1001/virtualmentor.2007.9.6.pfor1-0706&#10;..."
